100_jpg.rf.14fa87ff511c6790858ccbc03bf10be6.jpg,0,3,LOOPER_CATERPILLARS,Crop health log: Visible symptom — irregular brown lesions spreading along leaf veins with dark borders. Observation context: high humidity and warm temperatures favoured disease spread.
100_jpg.rf.14fa87ff511c6790858ccbc03bf10be6.jpg,1,2,LEAF_RUST,Tea bush inspection report: Disease symptom — orange felt-like algal spots with scalloped margins on shaded lower canopy leaves. Environmental note: incidence higher in gardens with high atmospheric humidity year-round.
107_jpg.rf.9c0264c78b1f4dfff87adea98349df8b.jpg,0,2,LEAF_RUST,Crop health log: Visible symptom — thallus-covered circular patches turning rusty brown with rough surface texture. Observation context: found predominantly on lower canopy leaves under heavy shade trees.
107_jpg.rf.9c0264c78b1f4dfff87adea98349df8b.jpg,1,2,LEAF_RUST,Diagnostic note: The sampled leaf shows velvety orange-red algal tufts scattered across the upper leaf surface. Background: common in old tea gardens with thick canopy cover and slow air movement.
